---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import ToConfirm from '../components/ToConfirm.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How The Elephant Path website handles your information: cookieless analytics, no trackers, and where clinical records are kept."
>
  <p>
    Your privacy matters to me. This policy explains what information this website collects, how it is
    used, and how it is protected. It covers this website only. Your clinical care is covered by a
    separate Notice of Privacy Practices, which you’ll receive when we begin working together. <ToConfirm
      note="TO CONFIRM: Notice of Privacy Practices provided via the portal"
    />
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    To understand how many people visit and which pages are useful, this site uses Cloudflare Web
    Analytics. It does not use cookies, does not track you across other websites and does not collect
    personal information such as your name or email address. <ToConfirm note="TO CONFIRM: analytics added before launch" />
  </p>

  <h2>No cookies, ads, or trackers</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising cookies, social media pixels (such as Meta or Google ad
    tracking), or other third-party trackers. The fonts are stored on this website, so no font service
    sees your visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Clinical records</h2>
  <p>
    If you become a client, your clinical records are kept in TherapyNotes, a secure, HIPAA-compliant
    electronic health record system, not on this website. Paperwork, secure messages, and statements are
    handled through the <ExternalLink href={site.links.clientPortal} newTab
      >TherapyNotes client portal</ExternalLink
    >. Telehealth sessions take place on Doxy.me, a secure, HIPAA-compliant video platform.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to other websites, such as the client portal, Doxy.me, Psychology Today, and crisis
    lines. Those sites have their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    Email is not always fully secure. Please don’t send health information by email. Once we begin
    working together, you can use the secure messaging in the client portal.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new date.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this policy, please call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>{
      site.email && (
        <>
          {' '}or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </>
      )
    }.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
